What is Intelligent Connected Instrumentation for Two-wheelers?
Intelligent Connected Instrumentation for Two-wheelers refers to an advanced human‑machine interface that combines digital display technologies with vehicle‑connectivity features such as Bluetooth, Wi‑Fi or cellular modules and embedded software platforms. The solution delivers real‑time vehicle data visualization, navigation display, smartphone integration, remote diagnostics and over‑the‑air updates, addressing limitations of traditional standalone dashboards. Upstream components include display panels, system‑on‑chip processors, connectivity chips and GNSS units; these are assembled into complete clusters for OEM deployment across motorcycles, electric two‑wheelers and scooters.
